@startuml
title OKS MCP Server — Concise Query Sequence

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor User
participant "Coding Agent /\nMCP Client" as Agent
participant "SSH local\nport forward" as SSH
participant "MCP Server\n127.0.0.1:8001" as MCP
participant "OksQueryService\n+ OksPipeline" as Service
participant "LLM API" as LLM
database "CVMFS TDAQ/OKS\ndata" as OKS

User -> Agent: Ask natural-language OKS question
Agent -> SSH: MCP request
SSH -> MCP: Encrypted forwarded request
MCP -> Service: oks_query(question, version)
Service -> LLM: Schema slice + translation prompt
LLM --> Service: Candidate OksQuery
Service -> Service: Validate and repair if needed
Service -> OKS: Execute approved read-only query
OKS --> Service: Filtered matching objects
Service --> MCP: Structured results
MCP --> SSH: MCP response
SSH --> Agent: Response through tunnel
Agent --> User: Explain result

note over Agent, MCP
  The architecture remains vertical.
  The sequence is intentionally concise:
  the agent owns conversation memory, while
  the server translates, validates, and executes.
end note
@enduml
